<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why Guyana Diaspora Guide exists: practical, honest guides for Guyanese living in the US, Canada, and the UK who handle business back home."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About Guyana Diaspora Guide</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="prose">
    <p>
      More than half a million people of Guyanese heritage live abroad — in Brooklyn and Queens,
      Scarborough, South Florida, and London. Between us, we send hundreds of millions of US dollars
      home every year, sponsor relatives, ship barrels, renew passports, and increasingly, buy land
      and build houses back home.
    </p>
    <p>
      Yet the practical information for doing any of that is scattered across outdated forum posts,
      word of mouth, and government pages that assume you're standing in Georgetown. Guyana Diaspora
      Guide exists to fix that: clear, current, step-by-step guides written specifically for
      Guyanese overseas.
    </p>
    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Money &amp; remittances</strong> — sending money home for the lowest real cost, and shipping barrels without wharf-day surprises</li>
      <li><strong>Immigration &amp; visas</strong> — family sponsorship, embassy interviews, and moving between Guyana and abroad</li>
      <li><strong>Passports &amp; documents</strong> — consulate services, GRO certificates, and keeping your Guyanese documents current</li>
      <li><strong>Property &amp; investing</strong> — buying land and building in Guyana safely from overseas</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Our approach</h2>
    <p>
      We don't do hype and we don't guess. Where fees, wait times, and requirements change often, we
      say so and point you to the official source. Nothing here is legal or financial advice — for
      high-stakes decisions, hire a licensed professional.
    </p>
    <p>
      Guyana Diaspora Guide is built by <strong>Savanna Studios</strong>, the team behind
      <a href="https://tasteofguyana.com">Taste of Guyana</a>. Questions or corrections?
      <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>

